title: date_sakazuki_2_part_1
location: office
---

{$name}: Yet another work day. Ah... I'm so tired, but the weekend is within sight. I'll just try my best and get plenty of rest later!
You get ready for work, then set off for the office. Once you arrive, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki is as strict as always, although you wonder if it's just your imagination or if he seems a little bit distracted.
5 o'clock rolls around and you jump out of your seat for a big stretch. Ahhhh... you feel so much better now! Time to head home, take a shower, rinse and repeat.
Walking down the long hall, you stop when you see a figure in white from afar. Is that...?
Wait a second... [shake]FLEET ADMIRAL SAKAZUKI?![/shake]
Has he clocked out at 5pm on the dot and not three hours later?! You've never seen him leave work earlier than you the entire time you've been here... You are almost concerned. Is Marineford under attack by pirates? Is there a war coming? Will you still have to come in tomorrow?!
You approach him, but he appears to be distracted, staring at something on the wall... You wave your hand but he doesn't acknowledge you at all. Maybe he hasn't noticed you yet? Or perhaps you are actually more stealthy than you thought? You decide to...
-> ... sneak up behind him to see what he's looking at.
    Keeping your footsteps as silent as a mouse, you inch closer and closer.
    Almost there... you can almost read the words on the shiny plaque on the wall...
    {$sakazuki}: Has anyone ever told you you shouldn't sneak up on Marines stronger than you, {$name}?
    You let out a squeak. He hasn't even turned around.
    {$name}: S-Sir!
    The Fleet Admiral now turns to look at you. He isn't impressed.
    {$sakazuki}: We have a habit of being hostile to anyone who sneaks up on us. It comes with how often pirates attempt to backstab. Either don't do it, or do it better.
    {$name}: I'm s-sorry.
    {$sakazuki}: ... Tch. So.
-> ... make yourself known and greet him.
    Gathering all your courage, you approach the intimidating man.
    {$name}: F-Fleet Admiral Sakazuki, sir!
    The Fleet Admiral glances at you.
    {$name}: Sir! Good evening!
    {$sakazuki}: ...
    {$sakazuki}: Likewise.
{$sakazuki}: What do you want?
You look toward the plaque he was looking at before you interrupted.
{$name}: I was surprised to see you leave work so early...
[Good ending last time] {$sakazuki}: I suppose it's a rare occasion. Pirates tend to occupy the majority of my time. //HOW DO??
[Neutral ending 1/ Neutral ending 2/ Neutral Ending 3 last time] {$sakazuki}: <pause>...Yes...? //HOW DO??
[Bad ending 1/ Bad ending 2 last time] {$sakazuki}: Hm. And yet somehow, I am not surprised to see you doing the same. //HOW DO??
{$name}: ...So I couldn't help myself. I noticed you were reading something...? May I ask what it is?
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: Names of all the current and past Heroes of the Navy. Most are dead, but not all. Vice Admiral Garp's name is on it.
{$name}: Oh...
You finally notice now, the fading names. There are so many. Was the Fleet Admiral just standing there reading mostly dead people's names? Isn't that kind of weird? Maybe he is looking for his name?
Is his name even on it? Does he care?
You take a deep breath...
-> ... and decide it's time for a tactical retreat. This is too weird.
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Nope_out>>
-> ... and choose to stay.
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Stay>>
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_Nope_out
location: office
---

{$name}: Well, sir, it has been an educational conversation but, um — I suddenly remember that I have... stuff to do at home. So I guess I'll just—
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$name}: Leave. I guess I'll just leave. You have fun here with your nameplates, sir.
You salute and walk away from the scene as fast as humanly possible. You glance behind you. Fleet Admiral Sakazuki hasn't stopped you. He doesn't pay you any further attention nor does he seem surprised.
Yeah, you totally made the right choice! Who would wanna stay after hearing that?! You go home and have an amazing warm bath, the event forgotten entirely.
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_Stay
location: office
---

{$name}: I didn't know that. That's... interesting. Wow, there are many names.
{$sakazuki}: Yes.
{$sakazuki}: It's less than a fraction of all those who have perished for the sake of Justice. Many go unnamed. But as long as your name is here, on this plaque, you'll be remembered by history.
{$name}: Well... I think you don't have to be remembered by ‘history' to matter! You can be remembered by your family and friends, too!
{$sakazuki}: [sad] You're right. There are many ways to be remembered. //HOW DO??
The Fleet Admiral traces his finger over a name you can't quite see from where you're standing. Suddenly, you're struck by curiosity.
{$name}: Do you have a family, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki?
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: ... Everyone has a family, {$name}.
{$name}: Um, well... is your name up there, Sir?
{$sakazuki}: No.
Ohhhh, you see what's going on now. You understand why he is here looking over these names if his name isn't on it. Clearly...
-> ... He's looking for a way to get himself remembered!
    {$name}: I know what you're doing! You want your name on it too, don't you, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki? That's really cool! You're ambitious!
    {$sakazuki}: <pause>...
    {$sakazuki}: No.
    {$name}: ...Wait... [shake]WHAT?![/shake] No way! Who wouldn't want to have their name remembered by everyone?! That'd be like... a promotion for a Fleet Admiral!
    {$sakazuki}: A promotion isn't everything, {$name}. It'd do you well to remember that.
    {$name}: B-But what about... glory? [shake]Happiness[/shake]?!
    {$sakazuki}: Do you genuinely think heroes of the Marines are happy people?
    {$name}: Well, Vice Admiral Garp seems pretty happy? He laughs all the time.
    {$sakazuki}: <pause>... If that is your measurement of happiness...
    {$name}: What does... what does that mean, Sir? I don't understand.
    But Fleet Admiral Sakazuki isn't interested in humoring you anymore. What did he mean? Vice Admiral Garp is happy... right?
-> ... He's admiring all these great past heroes!
    {$name}: Are you admiring all their names? They are like superheroes, aren't they! So cool...
    {$sakazuki}: <pause>...
    For a moment, you thought you said something wrong but then...
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki actually lets out a small laugh.
    {$sakazuki}: [smile] Yes, I suppose so. They *are* cool. They all did impossible feats.
    {$name}: Oh! Can you... when you have time, can you tell me about some of them?
    {$sakazuki}: [judging] <pause> Haven't you learned Naval history during your training? There's also a library within Marineford.
    {$name}: Yes, but it's better to hear from someone than to read from a book, right? It's more immersive, sir!
    {$sakazuki}: ... Perhaps.
    {$sakazuki}: It'd be good for Marines to know their names and what they've done, not just the glory, but the heartbreaks. The sacrifices for the greater good. Even their tragic ends.
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki taps the names.
    {$sakazuki}: Remember, {$name}, these aren't just heroic tales. They are also tragedies, and all the more admirable for it.
-> ... He has close ties with someone whose name is up there!
    {$name}: Do you know someone whose name is on the plaque, Sir?
    {$sakazuki}: ...
    {$sakazuki}: *Everyone* in Marineford knows Vice Admiral Garp, {$name}. The man is a menace.
    {$name}: I don't mean *him*. Well, I guess he counts too, but like... other people! Do you know anyone else?
    {$sakazuki}: ...
    {$sakazuki}: I know their stories.
    {$sakazuki}: Many wanted to make change.
    {$name}: Sir, that's not a real answer...
    But Fleet Admiral Sakazuki isn't interested in humoring you anymore. You try to puzzle out his words. You can't guess if that's a yes or a no.
{$sakazuki}: Enough reminiscence. I didn't leave work early just to stand here all night. I have actual errands to get to.
You realize this is your big break. The conversation you just had has so many hidden depths you find yourself failing to really understand half the things he told you. But this, this you know.
It is now time...
-> ... to make a run for it. He's giving you an out!
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Nope_out>>
-> ... to accompany Fleet Admiral Sakazuki and get to know him outside of work! Why not?
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Errands>>
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_Errands
location: office
---

{$name}: Errands? Oh! What a coincidence! I'm actually available for the rest of the evening. Please, let me tag along with you!
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: What kind of errands do you think I have?
Now that you think about it... you aren't sure. You decide you're just going to take a stab in the dark and hope for the best.
-> Like grocery shopping and stuff, right? I'm really good at haggling! I can help!
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Route_1>>
-> Like... official Marine... business... errands...? I'm sure Fleet Admirals... err... do that type of work...? Maybe?
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Route_2>>
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_Route_1
location: office
---

{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: Fine. I suppose a companion isn't the worst. You have proven to be reliable where it counted before.
Wow, you didn't actually think he would agree to it! You have no idea what to expect now. It's hard to imagine Fleet Admiral Sakazuki doing something as... *normal* as shopping.
It feels silly now that you actually take a few moments to think about it. Of course he has to eat. He's not a machine. But... what does he even eat? Fancy food? Lobster? Caviar? ~Truffles?~
You are kinda jealous. Being the Fleet Admiral must be *so* well paid. Maybe he's going to take you to a fancy place to do his shopping.
{$sakazuki}: Come, {$name}. The supermarket isn't far from the residential district. I don't want to spend all night walking there.
Of course, that makes sense. It does take a while to walk to the supermarket...
Wait a minute... the [shake]SUPERMARKET?![/shake]
Date Location: Town //HOW DO??
You look at the supermarket. It's... it's a supermarket. It's *the* Supermarket, in fact – the one everyone goes to get their groceries. You have visited it yourself many times before.
You aren't impressed. You thought he'd at least go to one of those fancy exotic places the higher ups go to. Apparently not?
...Maybe there's a hidden fancy area in this supermarket you have never explored before where Fleet Admiral Sakazuki goes to get his good stuff?
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki doesn't seem to notice your conflict, or maybe he doesn't care. He nods at the security guard who's waving at him. They know each other?! He's a *regular*?
{$sakazuki}: We don't have all evening, {$name}.
{$name}: U-Um, yes, Sir...
You walk into the underwhelming supermarket. You feel both like a silly tourist and like you are intruding on something incredibly private and forbidden as you follow the Fleet Admiral around. He grabs a few items here and there; a carton of eggs, a bag of coffee, some tea, toiletries...
Should you be here? Should you be seeing this? He feels scarily human.
{$sakazuki}: {$name}. *{$name}*.
{$name}: Y-Yes, sir?!
{$sakazuki}: You're spacing out. I thought you said something about helping me?
{$name}: I-I did, Sir! What do you need my help with?
{$sakazuki}: [Judging] Hmph. Since you have clearly missed half of it being in a daze, I have three zones left to go. The rice aisle, the produce area, and the garden section. Pick one. //HOW DO??
<<jump date_sakazuki_2_Grocery_shopping>>
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_Grocery_shopping
location: town
---

-> Rice aisle
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_rice>>
-> Produce area
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_peppers>>
-> Garden section
    <<jump date_sakazuki_2_plants>>
[To Zip: Can we make it so that players can only pick 2 options (and maybe they disappear once they have been picked so there can be no repeats?) out of 3? And then after 2 options, it leads to Lost_pet? Thank you very much!] //HOW DO??
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_rice
location: town
---

{$name}: Let's go with rice! Rice is a staple food!
{$sakazuki}: Rice it is.
You both go to the rice aisle. There are only a few shoppers around and none pay any attention to either of you. Fleet Admiral Sakazuki is looking at a bag of rice, squinting at the words written on it.
Well... you *are* curious. And maybe he won't scold you for being distracted if you actually engage with him.
{$name}: Fleet Admiral Sakazuki, Sir?
{$sakazuki}: ...Yes?
{$name}: So... do you... cook yourself?
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$sakazuki}: If that was your poor attempt at a joke, I'm not amused.
{$name}: Wha... no! I mean, like, cooking food, at home. Not like.. a joke about your powers!
{$name}: I wanted to ask if you made your own food.
{$sakazuki}: Hm.
{$sakazuki}: Yes.
{$name}: Oh... well...
-> Do you want to trade recipes?
    {$sakazuki}: <pause>[surprised] Trade recipes? //HOW DO??
    {$name}: Yeah, my Mom bakes! She taught me a few of her favorite recipes. I'm not as good a cook as I am a baker but I'm willing to learn!
    {$sakazuki}: ...
    {$sakazuki}: I don't make gourmet food. I cook everyday meals, with a lot of heat. Are you sure that's what you want?
    -> Eh... I'll pass... I thought you might know fancy recipes but nevermind.
        {$sakazuki}: I don't.
        {$sakazuki}: I value practicality. I don't have a lot of time in the day to begin with.
    -> That's perfect! I don't have time to make anything too complicated!
        <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
        Fleet Admiral Sakazuki scrutinizes you.
        {$name}: I'm serious, Sir! I can't spend hours a day making food. There's a reason I'm a Marine and not a baker.
        {$name}: I just want to switch up my meals, not cook for a dinner party.
        {$sakazuki}: <pause> Fine.
        {$sakazuki}: I'll pass along my own notes and recipes. They should be sufficient for daily situations.
        {$name}: Thank you very much, Sir! I appreciate it.
        {$sakazuki}: <pause>... You're welcome.
        {$sakazuki}: Lady Tsuru would approve.
        {$name}: Vice Admiral Tsuru, sir?
        {$sakazuki}: Yes. She taught us cadets that independence is a valuable trait.
-> Who taught you how to cook?
    {$sakazuki}: ...
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki stops, places the bag of rice down and stares at you for a long, uncomfortable minute.
    You do your best not to squirm under his stare.
    Another minute passes.
    {$sakazuki}: ... No one. I taught myself the skill.
    {$name}: I... see...
    {$sakazuki}: Why do you want to know?
    -> Cooking is hard. It takes a lot of patience to get it right!
        <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
        {$sakazuki}: ... It's a discipline. With enough training, you'll gain mastery.
        {$name}: Do you have mastery over it?
        {$sakazuki}: No.
        {$sakazuki}: It was necessary for me to learn at the time, but I don't have a passion for it. I learned enough.
        {$name}: That's still pretty cool though.
        {$sakazuki}: Thank you. It has earned its place in my life. Quite the calming activity, even if I have no desire to get fancy about it.
    -> You are famous, it's just weird you cook, I guess.
        <<set $sd2_points -= 1>>
        {$sakazuki}: Hm...
        {$sakazuki}: Is it?
        {$name}: Yeah! Not that I meant to call you weird, just in general I–
        {$sakazuki}: Being independent is an excellent reason to learn.
        {$name}: Well...
        Fleet Admiral Sakazuki is giving you a warning look you are somewhat more familiar with now. In the face of that, the other three Admirals typically only laugh and wave him off.
        You swallow.
        You are not that bold.
        {$name}: ...Yes, Sir...
        {$sakazuki}: I thought so.
-> But you are the Fleet Admiral, why don't you just hire people?
    <<set $sd2_points -=2>>
    {$sakazuki}:... And why should I do that?
    {$name}: I mean, you're filthy rich, right? Why should you have to do something so mundane?
    {$name}: If I were the Fleet Admiral, I would have people do everything for me. I wouldn't even lift a finger.
    {$sakazuki}: [frown] ... //HOW DO??
    {$sakazuki}: Then it is a good thing the line of choices for Fleet Admiral is long, and you are at the back end of it.
    {$name}: ... Wait... what does that mean?!
    {$sakazuki}: What do you think I *meant*, soldier?! Get a grip and examine why you are a Marine in the first place!
You stay silent, mulling over his words.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki finally makes his decision. Placing a few bags of rice in the cart, he glances at you.
Oh, he's letting you make a choice for the next destination. The next one should be...
<<jump date_sakazuki_2_Grocery_shopping>>
<<jump date_sakazuki_2_Lost_pet>>) //HOW DO??
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_peppers
location: town
---

{$name}: The produce area sounds nice. I like vegetables.
{$sakazuki}: Alright, that'll be our next destination.
The produce area isn't hard to locate. You look over different selections of vegetables and fruits before sneaking a look at Fleet Admiral Sakazuki. You wonder what he wants to buy.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki has gone straight to the peppers section. He holds up a red jalapeno and inspects it carefully before placing it aside. He picks up the next one, then the next, and another after that. The stack of red peppers grows in size. Still, he won't stop.
Is he buying a *month's* worth of red peppers?!
Finally, he moves away from them. You breathe a sigh of relief, but it's short-lived when he immediately walks straight to the chili peppers next, taking his time with those too!
{$name}: Wow, sir...
{$sakazuki}: What?
-> You must really like spicy food! I love peppers too!
    <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
    {$sakazuki}: Is that so?
    {$name}: Yeah! I like all types! Jalapeno, serrano and cayenne! I have never gone hotter than habanero though.
    {$sakazuki}: ... Spicy food is good.
    {$sakazuki}: I like red peppers with rice.
    {$name}: That sounds tasty!
-> Do you like peppers ‘cause you're hot, too?
    <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
    {$sakazuki}: No.
    {$sakazuki}: My coworkers have made those jokes often enough. I refuse to take them anymore.
    -> That was out of line. I'm sorry.
        <<set $sd2_points +=2>>
        {$sakazuki}: <pause>... It's fine. Do not tease others like that if you accompany them. They will get the wrong idea.
        Oh... he thinks you were teasing him. You want to tell him that you really do find him handsome, but you have a feeling it's not the right time.
        You keep the thought to yourself and let him finish picking his peppers.
    -> What joke, sir? I thought you liked to spice it ~up~? Because... spicy food? &&Geddit&&?
        <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
        Fleet Admiral Sakazuki groans, rubs the bridge of his crooked nose.
        {$sakazuki}: *I get it.* You are just as awful as the rest of the lot.
        {$name}: A lot that you might be exasperated by, but you still keep ~around~
        {$sakazuki}: For reasons no one knows. I certainly don't.
        {$sakazuki}: Enough joking around, I have to finish my shopping.
        {$name}: Sir, yes, Sir!
    -> Oh you misunderstood! It's not a joke! I was trying to say you're really sexy!
        <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
        {$sakazuki}: No.
        {$name}: Sir, I don't think–
        {$sakazuki}: I understand perfectly what you meant. *No.* We do not have that kind of relationship. Focus on being a good Marine and build up your skills.
        {$name}: ... Yes, Sir...
        {$name}: That was... out of line. I'm sorry...
        {$sakazuki}: <pause>... It's fine. Do not tease others like that if you accompany them. They will get the wrong idea.
        Oh... he thinks you were teasing him. You want to tell him that you really do find him handsome, but you have a feeling it's not the right time.
        You keep the thoughts to yourself and let him finish picking his peppers.
-> Aren't red peppers way below your paygrade?
    <<set $sd2_points -=2>>
    {$name}: With how many you're buying, one would think you just eat red peppers and nothing else!
    {$sakazuki}: And what's wrong with that?
    {$name}: I-I... well, it's really weird!
    {$sakazuki}: I won't apologize for how I live my life. If that inconveniences you, you can look away.
    {$name}: I'm s-sorry... that was out of line...
After a ridiculous amount of red peppers, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki appears... satisfied with his shopping. You hope that he doesn't actually eat them all in one go. Lava or not, that's going to burn a hole through his guts, and not in a good way...
{$name}: ... Is that all you need, sir?
{$sakazuki}: Hmm...
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki pauses, looks at his cart and then at the peppers still on the shelves. He picks up one last ghost pepper.
{$sakazuki}: We are done. Let's go to the next location.
{$name}: Yes, Sir! So that'd be...
<<jump date_sakazuki_2_Grocery_shopping>>
<<jump date_sakazuki_2_Lost_pet>>) //HOW DO??
===

title: date_sakazuki_2_plants
location: town
---

{$name}: How about the garden section? Flowers sound fun!
{$sakazuki}: Hm.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki makes his way to the garden section like someone who has frequented such a section many times before.
{$name}: So, err, do you come here often? Are you going to buy flowers for... somebody?
{$sakazuki}: ...
{$name}: ... No? Flowers for yourself, then?
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki holds up a bag of fertilizer.
{$sakazuki}: No.
The Fleet Admiral squints at the bag of fertilizer, trying to read the ingredients. He stops, places the bag down and looks at a shelf behind you. You turn around.
On the shelf are rows of carnivorous plants, all in horrible condition. They are wilted, their leaves blackened. They are clearly dying. And these irresponsible people didn't even put them away! You pick up a venus trap. Ugh, so horrendously overpriced, too!
These should've been in the trash, *yesterday*!
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki walks straight to the shelf of dying plants. He picks one up, examines it carefully. Places it down. Picks up another one. And then another.
{$sakazuki}: I'll take everything.
...
Everything? [shake]Everything?![/shake]
{$name}: Sir! You can't!
{$sakazuki}: <pause> Why not?
{$name}: Why not? [shake]Why not?[/shake] It's clearly a rip-off! These plants are dying.
{$sakazuki}: They are.
{$name}: Wait... wait a minute... if you already know they are *dying*, why do you still insist on buying them? They are priced way too high and–
{$sakazuki}: They are dying.
{$name}: That's what I *said*, Sir. I don't–
{$sakazuki}: If I don't take them, they will be *dead*.
The wind gets knocked out of you. You watch, a bit dumbfounded as Fleet Admiral Sakazuki gives the wilted plants a look of determination. He makes room in his cart and starts placing them inside. There's no talking him out of it.
You take a deep breath, watching him load plant after plant into the cart. Those plants are really way too overpriced...
-> You should at least help him!
    <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
    {$name}: Sir!
    {$sakazuki}: ... You're not stopping me.
    {$name}: I'm not planning to, Sir. I know you won't stop once you've decided on something. With that said...
    {$name}: I'm not going to let you be ripped off just because these people are irresponsible with their plants and didn't take care of them properly!
    Without thinking, you grab the Fleet Admiral by his wrist, tugging him toward an employee. He is surprised enough to let you do that.
    {$name}: Please look at these plants! They are all in terrible condition.
    Employee: Oh... oh, you're right, they are. I'm so sorry for the mistake, I'll bring out some good looking ones right away.
    {$name}: That's not why I'm here. He... Fleet Admiral Sakazuki, wants to take these off your hands.
    Employee: Oh... well, then...
    {$name}: Yes, that's why...
    -> Please consider a discount, given the condition of the plants!
        <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
        Employee: Well... that's...
        {$name}: Please! Think about it for a moment! You will just be throwing them away anyway! We will at least bring them home with us and you get something out of it!
        Employee: Well... I suppose... you have a point...
        {$name}: Thank you so much! We will take good care of these plants!
        The employee leaves for a moment to write up a note. You grin at the Fleet Admiral. You told him you were good at haggling!
        {$sakazuki}: You didn't have to do that...
        {$name}: Nope! But I want to help you. You were really worried about the plants, right? This is the least I could do.
        {$sakazuki}: Thank you, I appreciate it.
    -> I demand you give them to us for free!
        Employee: I'm sorry, we can't do that!
        {$name}:  But why not?! You are just going to throw them away anyway!
        Employee: Be that as it may, we can't give them away for free.
        Employee: I'm sorry, but if you want to get them, you have to pay for them. If you are unsatisfied with that, please put them back.
        The employee leaves in a huff. Damn. You are normally better at haggling than this. You give Fleet Admiral Sakazuki an apologetic smile.
        {$sakazuki}: You didn't have to do that...
        {$name}: Nope! But I want to help you. You were really worried about the plants, right? This is the least I could do.
        {$sakazuki}: <pause> Thank you, I appreciate it.
    -> Let me pay for them all!
        <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
        Without thinking, you grab the Fleet Admiral by his wrist, tugging him toward an employee. He is surprised enough to let you do that.
        {$sakazuki}: {$name}! What do you think you are doing?!
        {$name}: Sir, please let me help! I feel bad!
        {$sakazuki}: I don't need pity. You trying to stop your irrational guilt has nothing to do with me. I'll pay.
        He shakes you off and finishes putting the plants in the cart.
        You sigh. You lost and also made the Fleet Admiral angry.
-> Whatever, he's rich anyway. He has the cash to pay for it.
    You stand back and do nothing. Let him do whatever he wants. It's none of your business.
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki finishes inspecting all the venus fly traps and places them in his cart, seemingly unconcerned that he has just wasted a huge amount of money.
-> He's being unbelievably stupid! You should at least tell him he's being stupid!
    <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
    {$name}: Do you really not care?
    {$sakazuki}: <pause> Care? About what?
    {$name}: About wasting money! You're being deliberately obtuse! It's sad that these guys are dying, but no one can save them! You are fighting a futile battle!
    {$sakazuki}: <pause> Should these perceived futile battles not be fought?
    {$name}:... Well... yeah!
    {$sakazuki}: What if there is a one percent chance of winning? Do you still think it's a fight worth fighting for?
    -> One percent? Forget it! That battle is done for!
        <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
        {$sakazuki}: I hesitate to imagine you on the battlefield, {$name}.
        {$name}: Wait, what does that mean, sir?
        {$sakazuki}: You tell me. A battle with one percent odds of winning isn't worth fighting for. If pirates attack, and they are overwhelmingly strong, that battle is done for.
        {$name}: T-That's not fair, Sir! I'm just talking about nursing the plants being futile.
        {$sakazuki}: How you do small things is how you do everything. If you can't keep your code of conduct with the little things, do you actually think you can stick to your code with big things?
        {$name}: I-
        {$sakazuki}: *Enough.*
        Fleet Admiral Sakazuki says nothing else. You stand back and watch as the Fleet Admiral finishes inspecting all the venus fly traps and places them in his cart.
    -> Well... one percent is kinda awful... but I guess if one of these plants can be saved... then... yeah...? Still awful odds though.
