title: date_sakazuki_2_Lost_pet
location: town
---

...But before you two can leave, you are rudely interrupted.
There's a tiny white blur rushing past you, a furry *something* with a long leash attached to it.
You feel a yank around your ankles.
You look down. Too late!
The furry animal makes yet another mad dash, the sharp tug of the leash knocks you on your butt.
{$name}: [shake]OUCH![/shake]
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki bends down to pick up the struggling, wiggling furball while you sit up, glaring at the culprit.
{$name}: Ouch. That [shake]hurt.[/shake]
{$sakazuki}: You're a Marine. Deal with it.
Despite his words, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki offers you a hand. He appears distracted as he pulls you up, staring at his caught prize.
{$name}: What is that? I couldn't see it clearly.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki holds up the white furball before you.
It's... a dog. A tiny, fluffy dog. It's also wiggling in the Fleet Admiral's grasp, trying to break free from its confinement.
{$sakazuki}:  You need more training if a small dog can run you over, {$name}.
-> I-I did *not* get run over!
-> I knew my fall would've slowed it down long enough for you to detain it!
-> I'm sorry. I didn't pay attention to my surroundings! I'll train harder!
{$sakazuki}: ... Clearly.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki pats the dog once. He adjusts his grip so the wiggling furball will be more comfortable. He wraps the long leash around his arm.
{$name}: We haven't finished your shopping yet... what... what should we do with the furball, Sir?
{$sakazuki}: You are a Marine, aren't you? This is a crisis. What do *you* think we should do?
-> We have to find its owner, Sir! They must be so worried!
    <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
    {$sakazuki}: Shouldn't getting the shopping done come first?
    {$name}: Fleet Admiral...
    {$name}: Respectfully, Sir, I'll help get whatever you need later, but right now, the owner must be worried. It won't sit well with my conscience to do nothing about it.
    {$sakazuki}: Is that your final answer?
    {$name}: Yes, Sir! And if you don't agree with me then... well... well I'll just have to return the dog myself!
    {$sakazuki}: ... [smile] Very well. It is the more urgent situation of the two. I'll accompany you. //HOW DO??
    {$name}: Um... you're not... mad?
    {$sakazuki}: No.
    {$sakazuki}: Your words aren't without value. I have... friends... *a friend*... who would approve of such sentiments.
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki carries the dog in his palm while you look around for the distressed owner. It doesn't take long to spot a hysterical old lady asking people if they have seen a small dog.
    {$sakazuki}: Is this yours?
    Old Lady: Oh, thank you! Thank you so much!
    {$sakazuki}: You have to thank the person next to me. Here. Put a dog tag with an address on it next time.
    Without waiting for further words, Fleet Admiral Sakazuki turns around and walks away. You wave to the old lady and follow quickly after.
-> We should give it to the security guard at the door and finish your shopping.
    <<set $sd2_points +=2>>
    {$sakazuki}: And what's your reasoning behind it?
    {$name}: It'd be more efficient, Sir. We don't actually know how long finding the owner is going to take, and they most likely would seek help from an employee first. This way everything is resolved and there's no compromise on either task.
    {$sakazuki}: Hmm. Exactly like how I'd have done it. Excellent strategy, {$name}.
    {$name}: U-um, thank you, Sir.
    Fleet Admiral Sakazuki nods curtly.
    {$sakazuki}: You're welcome.
    You, like many others, have heard horror stories about the kind of things Fleet Admiral Sakazuki can do. Yet surprisingly, he's gentle with the animal in his hand. The dog appears content once it stops trying to run off, begging him for extra pets which he begrudgingly gives.
    He walks to the security guard to explain the situation and hands over the furball along with the leash.
-> We should definitely just leave the dog here! Someone's bound to find it eventually!
    <<set $sd2_points -=1>>
    {$sakazuki}: You think leaving it behind will solve the issue?
    {$name}: Well, yeah... why should we care about some random dog?
    {$name}: Plus, it tripped me! Mangy mutt! Hmph!
    The Fleet Admiral looks at you and then at the dog. You preen, feeling proud of your flawless solution.
    {$sakazuki}:... Disappointing. You chose to solve one crisis and ignore another, out of spite.
    {$name}: W-Well! What else can I do, Sir?!
    {$sakazuki}: We are handing this one to security. It should be the first place the owner seeks once they fail to locate the dog. Then we finish up the trip.
    You, like many others, have heard horror stories about the kind of things Fleet Admiral Sakazuki can do. Yet surprisingly, he's gentle with the animal in his hand. The dog appears content once it stops trying to run off, begging him for extra pets which he begrudgingly gives.
    He walks to the security guard to explain the situation and hands over the furball along with the leash.
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki wraps up the rest of the trip quickly while you follow after, mulling over what you have seen.
