        {$name}: Well, can we arrange it like a date? I can wear my best clothes...?
        {$sakazuki}: No.
        {$sakazuki}: Wear something practical. It's training.
        {$name}: Yes, Sir...
        {$sakazuki}: If that's all, we need to go. I have more business to handle.
        <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Balcony>>
    -> ...I don't see a lot of high ranking Marines train though. Do you still do your drills?
        <<set $sd2_points +=1>>
        {$sakazuki}: <pause>...
        {$sakazuki}: Not these particular sets of drills, but I still train to keep my skills sharp.
        {$name}: Oh... but you are already the Fleet Admiral. Doesn't that mean you are really strong?
        {$sakazuki}: In the Grand Line, there's a saying... a complacent Logia is a dead Logia. The fact of the matter is: a complacent anything in this sea is a dead man walking. The Grand Line is unkind to people without skill.
        {$name}: I-I see... that sounds scary...
        {$sakazuki}: Not as scary as you imagine. Training can be meditative. I enjoy the process.
        {$sakazuki}: We must go though. They are almost done and I have places to be.
        <<jump date_sakazuki_2_Balcony>>
